    "body": "**Problem:** Addrman groups peer addresses by network prefix or (when ASMap finds a match) by autonomous system.\nWithout ASMap, grouping classifies the address twice.\nWith ASMap, an IP lookup allocates a temporary key and the decoder calculates a shift distance for each mantissa bit.\nBuilding the group can also take several allocations for just a few bytes.\n\n**Fix:** When ASMap is disabled, skip the extra address classification in `GetMappedAS`.\nBuild ASMap lookup keys on the stack and decode integers by shifting each bit into the mantissa.\nReserve space for the address group before appending its bytes.\n\n**Time to group one IPv4 address:** (Raspberry Pi 5, ns per call, lower is better)\n\n```text\n                                 With ASMap                    Without ASMap\nmaster      baseline             ███████████████████▉ 1,982    █████▏ 518\n80a39cd417  Decode integers      ██████████████████▎  1,830    █████▎ 524\nadc7012941  Skip empty map       ██████████████████▎  1,824    ███▉   390\nbbe7b52765  Build lookup key     █████████████████▌   1,744    ████   394\n13e0803197  Reserve group space  ████████████████▍    1,640    ███▏   307\n```\n\nAcross the full series, `AddrManAdd` is 19.2% faster (59.1 to 49.6 ms).\n",
